east as sweet as a Beerenauslese."],["Trocken, Halbtrocken","Dry and medium dry. Under EU rules a dry wine has no more than 4 g of sugar a liter, or a little more when its acidity is high. Medium dry has more sugar than that."],["VDP, Grosses Gewächs (GG)","The VDP is an association of about 200 estates with rules stricter than the law. GG is its top dry wine from its best sites."]],"style":{"notes":["Baden, Germany's warmest region, makes wines that are usually fuller bodied and higher in alcohol than elsewhere in Germany.","Its Pinot Blanc and Pinot Gris are among the most powerful in Germany."]},"blurb":{"text":"Germany's third-largest wine region, in the southwest. Cooperatives and their members farm about two thirds of its vineyard area. Spätburgunder leads at 36% of the vines, then Müller-Thurgau, Grauburgunder and Weissburgunder."},"study":true,"levels":[3],"sources":[{"name":"Wikidata sitelinks and Wikimedia page views","url":"https://www.wikidata.org"},{"name":"Candiago et al. 2022, A geospatial inventory of regulatory information for wine protected designations of origin in Europe, Scientific Data (product specifications as of 2021)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01513-0"},{"name":"Fick and Hijmans 2017, WorldClim 2.1 monthly averages for 1970 to 2000, 2.5 minute grid (about 4.5 km)","url":"https://www.worldclim.org/data/worldclim21.html"},{"name":"Beck et al. 2023, High-resolution (1 km) Koppen-Geiger maps, Scientific Data (1991 to 2020)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02549-6"},{"name":"Winkler, Cook, Kliewer and Lider 1974, General Viticulture, University of California Press (heat summation regions)","url":null},{"name":"Jones 2010, Climate, grapes, and wine: structure and suitability in a variable and changing climate, VIII International Terroir Congress (which grapes suit which growing season temperatures)","url":"https://ives-openscience.eu/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Climate_Grape_Wine_Jones.pdf"},{"name":"Anderson, Nelgen and 